20,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,May,,"It seems our past trials for contactless payments and late-evening schedules were actually quite successful, though some lane-priority work failed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The staffing situation is precarious; the late-turn pool is thin and roadway crews are significantly under establishment.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Interestingly, the mid-city runs are slower, but the crowds clear at the same rate. Most delays are actually connection waits.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've found that work in pre-war shells is risky due to unrecorded voids, and ferry-rail data terms are still not agreed upon.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"We have a ring-fenced construction balance, but the technology budget is shrinking and ticketing fees are eating into our paving funds.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, if the crews are that thin, would a service extension be feasible?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, it would be a struggle. Overtime is already covering both final departures and overnight maintenance.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, does the lack of data agreement between ferry and rail make a unified system difficult?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, it certainly suggests a bureaucratic hurdle that isn't on any map.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, your mention of past trials is interesting. Did the late-evening pilot have a high cost?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, it actually met its cost-recovery target, which is a rare bright spot.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, if the delays are in the connections, perhaps we should focus on the flow rather than just the speed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The ""crowding"" complaints might be a symptom of waiting, not necessarily the volume of people.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, the construction balance you mentioned might be useful, but only if we avoid those pre-war voids.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"True, Shizue. But we must be careful not to commit to long-term fees we cannot sustain.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
