50,3,1,talk,May,,"The candidates are A: Integrated Fare Platform, B: Crosstown Bus Corridor, C: Station Access Upgrades, and D: Night Service Extension. I vote A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"D is impossible with the current rosters, and B needs roadway crews we don't have. I vote A.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Midori,,"B doesn't solve the connection issue, and C is too localized. A simplifies the start of the journey. I vote A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"C is too risky with the pre-war shells, and A has those data agreement issues. I'll vote for B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A's contractor fees are a worry, but B's paving costs are rising. D is a staffing nightmare. I vote A.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, why B? The earlier lane-priority stretches were returned to mixed traffic.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, the roadway crews are a third below establishment. Who would maintain the corridor?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, the timed runs show the mid-city is already slowing down.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I simply worry that A's ""integrated"" nature will stall in committee for years.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that is a fair concern, but the capital ledger's construction balance is better suited for something tangible.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,May,,"But A is a digital transition; it doesn't risk the ""voids"" Shizue found in the shells.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Exactly. It's the only one that doesn't rely on a depleted workforce.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Midori,,"And it addresses the ticketing friction, even if the audits show it's a small part of the delay.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I see your points. The staffing risk for D and the physical risk for C are indeed higher.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems A is the most viable, provided we manage the contractor fees.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
